Set up 7:45 pm, sun sets at 8:15. &nbsp;Outreach star party for The Nephrotic Syndrome Foundation.
www.nephroticsyndromefoundation.org
&nbsp;

When you arrive on&nbsp;Saturday, August 1, please enter through the main camp gate and proceed to the roundabout by the Dining Hall to check in with our Med Team. We kindly ask that you&nbsp;arrive by 7:30 p.m.&nbsp;to allow time for a quick COVID test before setting up.
For the safety of our immunocompromised campers, the test will be administered while you remain in your vehicle.&nbsp;Please stay in your car and refrain from interacting with other vendors, campers, or staff until your negative test result is confirmed&nbsp;(typically within 15&ndash;20 minutes).
We ask that you&nbsp;do not begin unloading or setting up until you've been cleared&nbsp;by our Med Team. Thank you for planning a little extra time into your arrival and for helping us maintain a safe and healthy environment for all of our Camp NSF families.
Required Forms*:
While waiting for your test results, please hand the Med Team:


Vendor Release Waiver


COVID/Health Waiver


*Each person attending as part of your team must submit their&nbsp;own&nbsp;forms.
&nbsp;
After Check-In:
Once cleared, you may head to the lawn, to setup.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
IMPORTANT Health Reminder:
Please attend&nbsp;only if you are 100% healthy.&nbsp;Even a mild illness can pose a serious risk to our medically vulnerable campers. If you or anyone on your team has been exposed to COVID within a week of camp or are feeling unwell, please do not attend. The COVID waiver includes a required disclosure of recent exposures.If you have questions or need to talk through anything, please don&rsquo;t hesitate to reach out.

The location is across the road from the Arroyo Road Staging Area. There is a locked gate at the entrance to the site, so you must let me know ahead of time if you plan to come, so we can make sure you have access.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

We have scheduled a&nbsp;Del&nbsp;Valle&nbsp;public outreach/club star party for August 15, 2026. &nbsp;Sunset is about 8:00. Set up starts at 7:30. The public portion of the event will go from 8:00 to 10:00 to accommodate the park closing time.
&nbsp;
The star party will be at the Arroyo Road Staging Area, just past 5055 Arroyo Road. This location is NOT at the&nbsp;Del&nbsp;Valle main entrance, but is on Arroyo Road (an extension of L Street), past the golf course and turnoff to Veterans Hospital.
&nbsp;
Weather permitting, we should have good views of the Moon (a small crescent that sets about 9:30) and the usual Summer deep sky objects.&nbsp; The location is fairly dark for being so close to Livermore.
&nbsp;
I hope we get several club members with scopes or binoculars. If you don&rsquo;t have a telescope or binoculars you want to share, please come out to enjoy the views.Please let me know if you plan to bring a telescope or binoculars, so I know how many to expect. We need several scopes to make this a successful event.&nbsp;
Thanks.&nbsp;
Coordinates:(37.6196638, -121.7528899)

